linux-cv181x-sodoport (7.0-9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial recipe-only Debian packaging for the Milk-V Duo 256M kernel.
  * Prepare uscan/gbp import flow for upstream Linux 7.0.
  * Seed the board kernel config from the local sg2002 Alpine packaging draft.
  * Add an initial DTS patch for the SG2002 Milk-V Duo 256M board.
  * Add a Debian-oriented config fragment scaffold for future config refreshes.
  * Rename the packaged kernel flavour to cv181x-sodoport.
  * Add a linux-source-cv181x-sodoport binary package.
  * Switch to Debian-style kernel packaging with a versioned image package,
    standard /boot artifact layout, and kernel maintainer hook integration.
  * Keep DTB installation generic and move board-specific u-boot-menu policy
    back out of the kernel package so board support packages can choose DTBs
    via U-Boot's fdtfile mechanism.
  * Keep packaged modules compressed with Zstd.
  * Fix DTB installation paths so synced /boot DTBs match u-boot-menu lookups.
  * Mark cross-build tools as native build dependencies so sbuild resolves the
    amd64 toolchain instead of trying to install them as riscv64 packages.
  * Replace debhelper-compat with a native debhelper dependency to avoid
    cross-resolver issues with the compat virtual package.

 -- Packaging Maintainer <maintainer@example.com>  Fri, 17 Apr 2026 23:10:00 +0900
